It's the stuff you need to ascend.  Generally, it's what you need
from the point of killing Rodney for the first time to offering the amulet.
Its contents vary by class and playing style, but typically, it includes:

+6/+7 weapon(s) (preferably artifact, although this is not necessary.  
I've ascended a tourist dual-wielding +7 crysknives) that you can use well
some method of ranged attack (spells, daggers, (cross)bows)
ring of free action
ring of levitation
blessed unicorn horn
blindfold/towel
dragon scale mail (gray or silver, usually)
amulet of reflection of life saving
cloak of magic resistance if you don't have another non-stealable source
   of MR, otherwise oilskin or elven cloak
speed boots
gloves of any type
helm of any type
shield, if you're not two-weaponing
some method of curse removal (spell, scrolls, holy water)
a goodly number of extra/full healing potions
wand(s) of death
wands of teleportation
sufficient food for the endgame
ring of confict (optional)
spare wish(es) (optional)
method of finding elemental portals (scrolls of gold detction, crystal
    ball, optional, but highly recommended)
method of digging through the earth plane (pick-axe, wands, spell if you've
    got ridiculuous amounts of energy)
bag of holding (optional)

Quite a bit of this is not applicable for monks, of course, but other 
than that, most ascentions seem to have the vast majority of this
stuff.

